  "body": "Adds a version panel, release announcements, and an in-place upgrade. 4.14.2 -> 4.15.0 (MINOR).\n\n## What it does\n\n- **Version panel** (Providers → Version): running version, latest release, last-checked time. Version also always visible in the sidebar.\n- **Announcement banner** when a newer release exists, linking to the release notes. Dismissal is remembered *per version*, so hiding 4.15.0 still surfaces 4.16.0.\n- **Update now** button, plus a manual **Check for updates**.\n\n## Design decisions worth reviewing\n\n**The upgrade mirrors `scripts/install.sh` rather than inventing a second install path** — download the wheel, verify SHA-256 against the digest GitHub publishes per asset, hand to `uv tool install --force`. A checksum mismatch aborts, exactly as the installers refuse.\n\n**Extras are preserved.** A naive reinstall would silently drop voice support. The uv receipt records extras and the Python pin, so both are carried across.\n\n**Upgrading does not restart the server.** A live process keeps serving already-imported code, so an upgrade can never truncate an in-flight stream. The caller gets a restart-required banner instead. This was the explicit tradeoff chosen over auto-restart.\n\n**Failure is expected, not exceptional.** Offline / rate-limited still renders the running version and keeps the last good payload, so the panel never blanks. The check is cached 6h and single-flighted.\n\n**Numeric version comparison** — 4.14.10 correctly outranks 4.14.9; lexical comparison would get this wrong. Unparseable versions never register as newer.\n\nThe install subprocess runs via `asyncio.to_thread`, so a multi-minute resolve doesn't block the proxy.\n\n## Security\n\n`/admin/api/version*` is loopback-gated like the rest of the Admin API. The subprocess uses a fixed argv (never a shell string), so release metadata cannot inject arguments.\n\n## Docs\n\nREADME refreshed with current dashboard screenshots, a new **Version & Updates** section, and a **Per-Key Attribution** section. The multi-key rotation section is corrected to describe the single-probe recovery and separate auth-lockout counter actually shipped in 4.14.x. Screenshots deliberately show only metadata — no request or response bodies.\n\n## Verification\n\n- 23 new tests: version parsing/comparison, cache + force, offline degradation, checksum-mismatch refusal (asserts the install is *never* invoked), extras preservation, failing-install reporting, missing-uv, and that the upgrade runs off the event loop.\n- Verified live against the real GitHub API on the running WSL server.\n- suppressions / ruff-format / ruff-check / ty all pass.\n\nThe v4.15.0 tag and wheel are already published so the installer-contract tests resolve.",
