    "message": "feat(admin): show the running version and install updates from the dashboard\n\nAdds a version panel, a release announcement banner, and an in-place upgrade.\n\nThe release check reads the GitHub releases feed on dashboard load, caches for\nsix hours, and collapses concurrent checks into one request. Failure is\nexpected rather than exceptional: offline or rate-limited still renders the\nrunning version and keeps the last good payload, so the panel never blanks.\n\nThe upgrade mirrors scripts/install.sh instead of inventing a second install\npath -- download the release wheel, verify its SHA-256 against the digest\nGitHub publishes, then hand it to ``uv tool install --force``. A checksum\nmismatch aborts, matching the installers' refusal. Extras recorded in the uv\nreceipt are carried across so an upgrade cannot silently drop voice support,\nand the Python pin is reused rather than guessed.\n\nUpgrading deliberately does not restart the server: a live process keeps\nserving the code it already imported, so an upgrade can never truncate an\nin-flight stream. The caller gets a restart-required banner and picks the\nmoment. The install itself is a slow subprocess and runs off the event loop.\n\nVersion comparison is numeric, so 4.14.10 correctly outranks 4.14.9, and an\nunparseable version never registers as newer.\n\nAlso documents the feature in the README alongside refreshed dashboard\nscreenshots, and corrects the multi-key rotation section to describe the\nsingle-probe recovery and separate auth lockout counter shipped in 4.14.x.",
